    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI consolidated the three separate duplicate checks (telephone, email, household) into a single derived **identity key** and now reject with 409 only on a whole-key collision.\n\n**The single definition** \u2014 `model/OwnerIdentity.java` (new): builds `identityKey = normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + (householdId or empty)`, with a `key(...)` builder and an `of(Owner)` convenience. This is the one place the key is defined; both the reject step and the response mapper use it.\n\n**One reject step** \u2014 `RejectDuplicateOwnerIdentity.java` (new) replaces `RejectDuplicateOwnerTelephone`, `RejectDuplicateOwnerEmail`, and `RejectDuplicateOwnerHousehold`. It derives the request's would-be household id, builds its identity key, and throws `DuplicateOwnerException` (\u2192 409) only when the *whole* key matches an existing owner's. Because the telephone is part of the key, same-household members with different telephones now get distinct keys and are both allowed.\n\n**Shared household logic** \u2014 added `OwnerHouseholds.assignedId(...)`, the single rule for the household id an owner would receive. Both `RejectDuplicateOwnerIdentity` (before build) and `AssignOwnerHousehold` (at save) now call it, so the key used for rejection matches the id later stored.\n\n**Pipeline** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml` now runs `normalizeTelephone \u2192 normalizeEmail \u2192 rejectDuplicateIdentity \u2192 build` (both fields normalized before the single check; the check stays ahead of build so no customer-code sequence is consumed on a rejected request).\n\n**Return identityKey** \u2014 added a read-only `identityKey` to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml`, populated via `OwnerMapper.identityKey(owner)` \u2192 `OwnerIdentity.of(owner)`, consistent with the other derived fields.\n\n**Removed** the three obsolete reject functions, their three exceptions + handlers, and three escalation YAMLs; added `DuplicateOwnerException` + handler + escalation YAML in their place.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreRejectsIdentityCollision` \u2014 same telephone \u2192 409) and the full suite pass.",
